/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/gpt.md:49:[COPIED-AUTHORITY] C3View is deterministic conditional on captured predecision inputs. Detached Q1/Q2 can inherit ordinary observation-time SINR ancestry; detachment removes gradients, not ancestry. Direct SINR tokens, fresh encoder draws, privileged teacher outcomes, and postdecision information are forbidden. Deployment retains one scalar Q3, one common native safe mask, and one literal masked \(Q1+Q2+Q3\) argmax without coordination or repair (`authority/LC-SRS-GATE-CONTRACT.md`, §3).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/gpt.md:100:[PROPOSAL] **Method and comparators.** Preserve LC-SRS, \(\lambda=118424222.8550065\) bit/J, \(\kappa=10097071012.757404\) bits, their frozen hexadecimal representations, C3View, 67–64–64–1 scorer, optimizer, S/R/C loss, and 2,000 updates. Fit INFORMED and MATCHED-PLACEBO only: 48 models. Retain ZERO-SURFACE \(B=Q1+Q2\) and TEACHER-ORACLE diagnostics. Preserve gate §7’s training-world strata, cyclic permutations, unchanged held-out labels, and ≥80% placebo eligibility per fold. No sign-reweighted training or candidate variants.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/C3-PANEL-HARNESS-2026-09-10.md:72:For the smoke, each trained model runs the production Q1+Q2 proposal. Because all eight raw proposals failed the unchanged “served-user count must not decrease versus BASE” guard after only two smoke epochs, each ran the production deterministic repair against exact guarded support. Each then built its own `bounded-union-v2` catalogue around the repaired seed. The eight learned catalogues each had 911 rows; the external baseline catalogue had 1,004. The smoke happened to produce only two physical seed families—one learned family and BASELINE—so it is not evidence of the disjoint catalogues observed in the supporting audit. All nine authenticated scored-catalogue hashes were distinct.
