The code-file digest is
`25c4bd512423d618eb2977d3aed9eb471f183a7b31f8323157834d96fbbd9911`.
It follows the Q1-v2 shape: pure state projection, authenticated row/shard
versions, canonical digests, a public-geometry resolver, and exact/primitive
builder adapters. No sealed source or artifact was modified.

### Original-slot disposition

| sealed slot | disposition | reason |
|---:|---|---|
| 6 | removed | exact function `1[background occupancy > 0]`; this also removes the Q2 copy that Q1-v2 had already removed from Q1 |
| 10 | removed | exact function `1[offset_1 mean SE > 0]` |
| 14 | removed | exact function `1[offset_2 mean SE > 0]` |
| 18 | removed | exact function `1[offset_3 mean SE > 0]` |
| all other 18 | retained exactly | projection audit maximum absolute difference `0.0` |

[RUN] The three sealed constants are retained, explicitly documented, and not
counted toward effective dimension:

- Old slot 8 `required_power_cap_margin` is computed by the exact builder as
  `BEAM_RF_CAP_W − profile.required_power_w_max`; it is zero because every
  retained exact-path rate profile on this development panel saturates the
  cap. It remains meaningful on a panel with nonsaturating profiles.
- Old slot 9 `missing_incumbent` is zero because every measured development
  anchor/user has an incumbent physical mapping. It remains meaningful for a
  tape with an unserved prior mapping.
- Old slot 19 `offset_3_survival` is zero because no focal action change in
  development steps 0–9 remains physically served at the third offset. It is
  retained because survival is directly consumed by C2's absorbing failure
  rule and is not structurally zero on the declared schema's full domain.

### Added coordinates and no-proxy rule

[DERIVED] The C2 target accumulates physical surplus while alive at offsets
1–3, turns the first invalid/non-surviving offset into a loss, and makes every
later offset an absorbing loss. Focal-link elevation at each of those exact
three offsets is therefore decision-time forecast geometry for link
visibility/persistence—the quantity C2 predicts—not a feature added because
it helped Q1.

[RUN] The resolver obtains satellite and user ECEF positions from the declared
forecast-horizon provider at boundary 0 for `step+1`, `step+2`, and `step+3`,
then computes physical elevation. Provider-array cross-check errors were at
most `5.400e−13°` in world 1 and `2.842e−13°` in world 2 during full checkpoint
projection. The direct exact-adapter audit error was `3.695e−13°`.

[RUN] No non-derivable proxy was introduced. Null action has no focal physical
link and therefore uses three explicit zeros; all non-null rows use provider
geometry. Each added normalized elevation has 7,597 exact values and is
nonconstant.

### Successor dimension

[RUN] Q2-v2 has serialized width `21 = 22 − 4 + 3`. Its only constants are
successor slots 7, 8, and 17 (the three retained constants above); it has no
remaining exact nonconstant equal/indicator relation. Both centered and
uncentered rank are `18`, and semantic effective dimension is **18**. Full
condition numbers remain infinite because of retained constants; the
nonzero-subspace condition numbers are `1529.0419` uncentered and `739.8939`
centered.

