/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/C2-WIRING-2026-09-10.md:1:**The C2 term does reach the FACTORIAL catalogue-row score, and it first changes a choice at the exact multiplier `k = 1602647948148653845449188374968356494 / 92924733498620994020746630350594813 = 17.246731712956027…`.**
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/C2-WIRING-2026-09-10.md:3:# C2 wiring diagnostic — 2026-09-10
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/C2-WIRING-2026-09-10.md:9:**PASS: the wiring is live.** The three exact equalities in `ORACLE-FACTORIAL-2026-09-10.md` are not the signature of a disconnected C2 arm in this runner. On the real catalogue, C2 is sparse and dominated when C1 is present: it is exactly zero on 96.3736% of eligible rows, every selected row is an association/C1 row whose C2 term is exactly zero, and C2 must be multiplied by about 17.25 before any one of the eight per-anchor choices changes.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/C2-WIRING-2026-09-10.md:11:This is not merely a source-reading conclusion. A source-shaped synthetic fixture was passed through the actual FACTORIAL `compact_anchor` and `choose_for_anchor` functions. `DROP_C2` selected the association row (index 1), while `FULL` selected the control row (index 2).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/C2-WIRING-2026-09-10.md:15:## Q1 — Does C2 reach the score?
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/C2-WIRING-2026-09-10.md:22:4. FACTORIAL identifies a row with `mode_offsets_by_user` as control-changed and classifies it as `route_kind = "C2"` (`/home/sat/mcrl-v025-arch-ws/scripts/run_oracle_factorial.py:199-231`). It forms C2's numerator and energy deltas from the additive profile minus the incumbent (`run_oracle_factorial.py:234-247`).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/C2-WIRING-2026-09-10.md:23:5. The arm declaration includes C2 in `FULL` and excludes it in `DROP_C2` (`run_oracle_factorial.py:54-62`). `pseudo_values` iterates those declared terms and adds both the route numerator and energy delta (`run_oracle_factorial.py:361-367`); `choose_for_anchor` then computes the row score `n - eta*e` and takes its exact argmax (`run_oracle_factorial.py:370-383`).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/C2-WIRING-2026-09-10.md:25:Therefore `FULL` and `DROP_C2` differ by a C2 term that is **computed and used**, not computed then discarded and not absent.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/C2-WIRING-2026-09-10.md:27:There is an important support restriction. FACTORIAL rejects eligible mixed association/control rows (`run_oracle_factorial.py:203-220`) and writes C2 as zero unless the row is classified as C2 (`run_oracle_factorial.py:239-246`). Thus the live C2 term is structurally zero on every C1 row; this is deliberate in this exact decomposition, not a dropped value.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/C2-WIRING-2026-09-10.md:31:The replay used the common exact converged price of `FULL` and `DROP_C2`, `eta = 9.029225860975936… Mbit/J`, and computed each row's score contribution as
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/C2-WIRING-2026-09-10.md:33:`C2(row) = delta demand-capped bits(C2,row) - eta * delta energy(C2,row)`.
