### Why the two geometry fields are not sufficient

The provider computes decision-boundary direct nominal gain as

`transmit_gain_linear(off_axis_angle) * nominal_path_without_scintillation(slant_range, elevation, peak_receive_gain)`

at [`provider_legacy.py:717`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/provider_legacy.py:717) through [`provider_legacy.py:734`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/provider_legacy.py:734). The path factor explicitly consumes both `slant_km` and `elevation_deg` ([`provider_legacy.py:488`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/provider_legacy.py:488)); its underlying link budget computes total path loss from both quantities ([`link_budget.py:664`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/src/mcrl/env/link_budget.py:664)). Q1-v2 supplies off-axis angle and elevation but not slant range, satellite position/altitude, or an equivalent path factor. Q2 supplies none of those direct geometry primitives. Hence the union of Q1-v2 and Q2-v1 is not a sufficient set from which the head can compute the exact per-option `nominal_gain` used by `RSS_MAX`.

## Derived on paper

- `nominal_gain > 0` by provider contract, so `10 log10(nominal_gain)` is strictly monotone and preserves every per-user option ranking. One such scalar per legal option is sufficient to express `RSS_MAX`; raw watts-per-watt would also work.
- Fixed positive schema scaling also preserves scalar ordering. Therefore adding the scalar to either Q1 or Q2 is enough for an expressive scoring head; adding it to both is unnecessary for this narrow expressibility repair.
- Adding `slant_range` instead would complete the physical primitive set only for Q1-v2 (off-axis + elevation + slant plus frozen link-budget constants). It is less minimal and makes the head learn the nonlinear antenna/path formula. Direct log-gain is the smallest robust field.

## Inferred design judgment

The binding issue for exact `RSS_MAX` imitation is **features/representation**, not optimisation: the current head inputs omit the decisive per-option scalar (and, even under Q1-v2, omit the last primitive needed to reconstruct it). Training longer or changing the schedule cannot make an invariantly absent quantity available. Adding this field would create a new feature schema and require a compatible successor plus retraining; it must not mutate the sealed schemas/checkpoints in place.

One nuance does not change that conclusion: the non-exact provider-primitive fallback approximated candidate margin using a log gain ratio ([`run_v025_pilot_c3.py:403`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py:403), [`run_v025_pilot_c3.py:415`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py:415)). The named frozen run and v2 corpus lineage are exact-view based, and the schema contract itself does not promise that fallback-only monotone encoding. It cannot establish representability for the learned system under audit.
